ption {:value "255688"} "Kayak Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255714"} "Kayak Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255727"} "Kayak Fours, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255739"} "Canadian Singles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255751"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255757"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255763"} "Canadian Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255769"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "255775"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "255782"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255468"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "255607"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "255809"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "255953"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256092"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256226"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "256337"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258763"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008517"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/162"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "6 – 10 August 1984"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/604"} "Lake Casitas, Los Padres National Forest, California"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/255701"} "42 from 21 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Unlike the 1980 American-led boycott, which had had a limited impact on the canoeing events, the Soviet boycott of the 1984 Summer Olympics severely depleted the field in the sport. This was noticeable in the men’s K-2 500, as nations that had won two of the last edition’s medals and six of the last nine World Championship medals (including all of the gold ones) were absent. This left three pairs who had medalled recently at major international tournaments: Canadians " [:a {:href "/athletes/9268"} "Hugh Fisher"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9299"} "Alwyn Morris"] " (bronze at the 1983 World Championships), twin brothers " [:a {:href "/athletes/9981"} "Matthias"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9982"} "Oliver Seack"] " of West Germany (bronze at the 1982 World Championships), and Spain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9503"} "Herminio Menéndez"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9482"} "Guillermo del Riego"] " (silver at the 1980 Summer Olympics). Additionally, New Zealand’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10436"} "Paul MacDonald"] " had been runner-up at the 1982 Worlds with " [:a {:href "/athletes/10442"} "Alan Thompson"] ", but was partnered with " [:a {:href "/athletes/10430"} "Ian Ferguson"] " in Los Angeles."] "\n\n" [:p {} "New Zealand won its opening heat against the Swedish duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/10752"} "Per-Inge Bengtsson"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10787"} "Lars-Erik Moberg"] ", the latter of whom had already been runner-up to Ferguson in the K-1 500 by the time of this event’s final. West Germany, meanwhile, was third in Canada’s heat, behind the Italian pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/10207"} "Daniele Scarpa"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10212"} "Francesco Uberti"] ", while Spain came in fourth in a heat won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/9781"} "Andrew Sheriff"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9789"} "Jeremy West"] " of Great Britain and advanced only through the repêchage, only to be eliminated in the semi-finals. New Zealand, Canada, and Great Britain were the victors in that round, while Ferguson and MacDonald continued their streak by capturing gold in the final with over a second to spare. The remaining podium spots came down to a battle between Sweden, Canada, Italy, and Romania’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10586"} "Nicolae Fedosei"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10626"} "Angelin Velea"] " who finished in that order with only 0.34 seconds between them. Ferguson and Moberg would continue their feud the next day in the K-4 1000, where the New Zealanders were once again victorious and forced the Swedes to settle for silver, while the Canadians would continue their streak by winning Canada’s second Olympic title since 1936, with the first having come the day before from " [:a {:href "/athletes/9258"} "Larry Cain"] " in the C-1 500."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Rep"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "126/128"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10430"} "Ian Ferguson"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/10436"} "Paul MacDonald"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NZL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NZL.png"}] "NZL"]] [:td {} "1:36.82 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:36.10 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:34.21 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "150/153"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10752"} "Per-Inge Bengtsson"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/10787"} "Lars-Erik Moberg"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "1:37.12 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:37.82 (3 h3)"] [:td {} "1:35.26 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr